From: piano-fedora <dev@piano.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: end active transfers before halting the device controller

The product retires the USB owner from the kernel's ExitBootServices call.
When a host is enumerating the device at that moment, Halt() clears DCTL
RunStop while EP0 still has a transfer posted and only polls DSTS DevCtrlHlt
for 100 ms, so the core never reports the halted state and the whole boot
fails with EFI_TIMEOUT.

Real-device log on a 25091RP04C:

  SUNUEFI_USB_SERVICE_CLEANUP stage=begin ... dctl=80F00000 dsts=0000C858
  SUNUEFI_USB_SERVICE_CLEANUP stage=halt status=Time out dctl=00F00000 dsts=...
  PIANO_START_FAILED stage=MENU handoff=linux-uki status=Time out

DSTS at the failure shows an attached link in the Address state, and an
earlier boot with the same cabling logged SUNUEFI_USB_EPCMD_TIMEOUT for an
EP0 SET_ADDRESS command. The host was mid-enumeration and the firmware was
not servicing it.

The databook (4.1.8, table 4-7) requires the software to send DEPENDXFER for
active transfers before clearing RunStop; dwc3_gadget_soft_disconnect() does
exactly that, and dwc3_gadget_run_stop() additionally keeps the HS/FS PHY
interface awake across the transition and allows about two seconds for
DevCtrlHlt. Mirror both here: end the posted transfers through the existing
StopTransfer(), clear GUSB2PHYCFG SUSPHY/ENBLSLPM for HS/FS around the stop,
and give the core two seconds instead of one hundred milliseconds.
---
diff --git a/uefi/core/PianoDwc3Device.c b/uefi/core/PianoDwc3Device.c
index 1d45a5a..98421ac 100644
--- a/uefi/core/PianoDwc3Device.c
+++ b/uefi/core/PianoDwc3Device.c
@@ -249,10 +249,21 @@ STATIC EFI_STATUS Command(UINT8 Ep,UINT32 Cmd,UINT32 P0,UINT32 P1,UINT32 P2) {
   if(Saved)Dw(0xC200,Phy);
   return EFI_TIMEOUT;
 }
+STATIC EFI_STATUS StopTransfer(UINT8 Ep);
 STATIC EFI_STATUS Halt(VOID) {
+  // Databook 4.1.8: a device-initiated disconnect must end every active
+  // transfer before RunStop is cleared, or the core can stay in a transfer
+  // state and never report DevCtrlHlt. A host that re-enumerates while the
+  // loader reads its image leaves EP0 armed, which is where this timed out.
+  for(UINTN Ep=0;Ep<ARRAY_SIZE(mPending);++Ep)if(mPending[Ep])(VOID)StopTransfer((UINT8)Ep);
+  // dwc3_gadget_run_stop keeps the HS/FS interface awake across the stop.
+  UINT32 Phy=Dr(0xC200),Saved=mControl.SuperSpeed?0:Phy&(BIT6|BIT8);
+  if(Saved)Dw(0xC200,Phy&~Saved);
   Dw(0xC704,Dr(0xC704)&~BIT31);
-  for(UINTN I=0;I<10000;++I){if(Dr(0xC70C)&BIT22)return EFI_SUCCESS;gBS->Stall(10);}
-  return EFI_TIMEOUT;
+  BOOLEAN Halted=FALSE;
+  for(UINTN I=0;I<2000;++I){if(Dr(0xC70C)&BIT22){Halted=TRUE;break;}gBS->Stall(1000);}
+  if(Saved)Dw(0xC200,Phy);
+  return Halted?EFI_SUCCESS:EFI_TIMEOUT;
 }
 STATIC EFI_STATUS CompleteEventDma(PIANO_DMA_BUFFER *Buffer) {
   EFI_STATUS S=PianoDmaComplete(Buffer,EFI_SUCCESS,TRUE);
